// The server's own program, its guard: every file of the package but the
// tests, with no Bun and no Node types, and a `lib` of `ESNext` only. `tsc`
// follows imports, so a file passes only if all that it imports passes too.
// It lists two files of declarations: the core's, `../core/tsconfig.core.d.ts`
// (what the core may use, so that a file that imports the core passes), and
// the server's own, `tsconfig.server.d.ts` (what a file of the server uses
// beyond that). So the guard refuses a module of Bun or of Node that no
// declaration names, and passes what those declarations name, the core's
// `node:crypto` too. What refuses each module of Bun or of Node in the
// server's files is the list of built-ins of `tools/graph.ts` (`BUILTINS`),
// which gives them none. The tests are checked with the Bun types, by
// `tsconfig.test.json`.
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ESNext"],
    "types": []
  },
  "files": ["../core/tsconfig.core.d.ts", "tsconfig.server.d.ts"],
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts"]
}
